---
title: Why speak first in the midst of chaos
date: 2025-01-01
tags: []
provenance:
  journal: Indelible Literary and Arts Journal
  year: "2025"
---
To prove that my breath is reality

A private voice whispers\
then burns\
in wasted sacrifice\
A voice in protest\
now ash in a tray\
The lack of this voice now\
bleeds inside me\
until it bursts\
into a voice too late\
too weak

This is a familiar view.\
A nation writhes\
from internal bleeding\
bombs burst to nurse it.\
I hold it at a distance.\
Disown it like an expired match.

Why speak first in the midst of chaos?\
To be ubiquitous\
To never burn away
